1
00:00:01,060 --> 00:00:02,100
There it is.

2
00:00:02,340 --> 00:00:04,693
The old man's ship is right on schedule.

3
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:07,002
He's just about 20 minutes away.

4
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,517
So as far as you know, Mr.

5
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:10,377
Joestar's the only passenger on board?

6
00:00:10,460 --> 00:00:11,290
He is.

7
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:15,317
The rest of the crew members are
from the Speed Wagon Foundation.

8
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:16,260
Even so,

9
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:18,437
I'm sure Chili Pepper
will try to pass over

10
00:00:18,520 --> 00:00:21,108
the water and sneak
onto the old man's ship.

11
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:25,207
Despite the fact that he's
confined to areas with electricity.

12
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:28,597
If he gets to Joseph first, he'll
kill him without a second thought.

13
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:32,057
and everything we've gone through
will have been for nothing.

14
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:33,100
Hey, Jotaro!

15
00:00:33,420 --> 00:00:35,557
We checked the boat over
and it's good to go!

16
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:37,287
We also checked the battery.

17
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:39,077
There's no sign of him in here.

18
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:41,637
We're ready to set out
whenever you give the word.

19
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:42,550
About that.

20
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:46,288
Only Okuyasu and I are heading
over to meet with the old man.

21
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:49,897
I want you to stay here and
hold down the fort with Koichi.

22
00:00:49,980 --> 00:00:50,810
Stay here?

23
00:00:50,893 --> 00:00:52,517
But you'll need backup, won't you?

24
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:53,720
Yeah, he's right!

25
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:55,477
Josuke, Chili Peppers' user,

26
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:58,597
is hiding somewhere in this
harbor watching our every move.

27
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:02,737
Understand he's laying
low right now and waiting

28
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:04,997
for us to do something
that'll give away the ship's

29
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:10,337
position and my gut's telling
me a boat won't be his

30
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:13,717
hiding place all he needs to
make it over to the old man

31
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:16,337
is a battery and something
faster than a speed boat

32
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:19,817
once he puts those two things
together he'll use it to

33
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:22,617
send chili pepper flying
to the old man's ship wait

34
00:01:22,700 --> 00:01:25,437
a second are you thinking
he's gonna take to the sky?

35
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:26,350
Yeah.

36
00:01:26,433 --> 00:01:30,000
To be perfectly frank, he's
probably making off with a remote

37
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:32,217
controlled plane as we speak.

38
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:34,037
That thought hadn't even occurred to me!

39
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:35,260
But it's possible.

40
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:39,957
Once they pick up speed, model airplanes
can fly over 100 kilometers per hour!

41
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:42,077
Faster than the motorboat's top speed!

42
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:46,917
And because Chili Pepper will be in control
of it, he can fly the plane as far and

43
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,557
as high as the battery will take him!

44
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:50,993
He doesn't need a remote control signal!

45
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:52,100
Listen, Josuke.

46
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:56,928
If If you spot anything flying around
here, I want you to search for the user.

47
00:01:57,220 --> 00:02:01,044
Koichi's reverb has a range of 50
meters, so he can help out too.

48
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:06,217
If that stand gets to the ship before
we do, the old man is as good as dead.

49
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:09,937
Your job is to stay on watch and
protect your father from the harbor.

50
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:11,160
We clear Josuke.

51
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:12,630
Yeah.

52
00:02:12,713 --> 00:02:15,657
From here on out, we don't
have a single second to spare.

53
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:17,505
Joestar's life is on the line.

54
00:02:30,780 --> 00:02:33,580
Thank you.

55
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:39,060
Best of luck, Okuyasu.

56
00:03:43,880 --> 00:03:45,360
Sing to you, Koichi.

57
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:04,997
In about 20 minutes, we'll finally
arrive at the Port of Mariah, Mr.

58
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:05,910
Joestar.

59
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:08,140
Is that right?

60
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:13,440
I seem to have misplaced my cane.

61
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:14,780
Have you seen it?

62
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:18,432
Isn't that it right in front of you, sir?

63
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:28,900
So he's my father, huh?

64
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:33,130
Josuke?

65
00:04:33,213 --> 00:04:34,081
Are you alright?

66
00:04:36,380 --> 00:04:37,700
I'm just processing.

67
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:39,937
I've never met this guy in my life.

68
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:42,785
Yet I'm supposed to accept
that he's my father.

69
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:45,180
I don't know, it's...

70
00:04:52,860 --> 00:04:55,637
But the only thing that
matters right now is his life

71
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:58,577
is in danger if I didn't
even lift a finger to help.

72
00:04:58,660 --> 00:05:03,340
I'd always regret it besides my mom
would fall apart if the guy croaked.

73
00:05:05,860 --> 00:05:11,540
Damn that Jotaro if he left you two mouth
breathers behind to sniff out my user.

74
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:16,475
That means he completely saw through
my remote controlled playing trick.

75
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,920
There you are Chili Pepper.

76
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:28,600
I'll give this to Jotaro Kujo,
the man's sharp as a tack.

77
00:05:31,220 --> 00:05:33,632
He's the last person I'd want finding me.

78
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:35,240
He'd just kill my five.

79
00:05:36,120 --> 00:05:37,296
Speaking of killing,

80
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:39,857
this remote-controlled
Spitfire plane can reach

81
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:42,587
Joseph Joestar's boat
in a mere five minutes.

82
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:47,680
A dinged-up old motorboat, on the other
hand, would take about eight to ten.

83
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:49,030
Meaning,

84
00:05:49,113 --> 00:05:52,077
if I can put you two down for
a dirt nap in three minutes,

85
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:54,297
it'll give me time to
catch up and pass them.

86
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:57,237
Wait, are you trying to tell
me you're Silly Peppers, user?

87
00:05:57,320 --> 00:06:00,340
You're looking at Akira Otoishi, age 19.

88
00:06:00,780 --> 00:06:03,309
Oh, and don't let the
guitar throw you off.

89
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:09,744
One day I want to be a rocking guitarist,
the likes of Jimi Hendrix and Jeff Beck.

90
00:06:09,860 --> 00:06:13,497
That's why I keep this sweet little
mama on my person 24 hours a day,

91
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:14,639
seven days a week.

92
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:18,753
One day the masses will look
up from their mundane lives.

93
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:23,649
And they'll be lining up for miles to
let my music knock them off their feet!

94
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:30,057
People around the world will know my name.

95
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:31,600
Oh yeah?

96
00:06:33,940 --> 00:06:34,977
This can't be good!

97
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:38,236
I never thought a stand user
would come out of hiding.

98
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:41,177
Which means there's no doubt
in his mind that he can

99
00:06:41,260 --> 00:06:44,201
slaughter both me and
Josuke without much trouble.

100
00:06:46,620 --> 00:06:51,326
I'm ready for round two with Shining
Diamond, but I'll only use my little pinky,

101
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:53,380
just like I did with Okuyasu.

102
00:06:53,820 --> 00:06:55,467
You should get back, Koichi.

103
00:06:58,820 --> 00:07:01,100
It's game on, Josuke Higashikata!

104
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:02,640
Just a minute. Huh?

105
00:07:02,980 --> 00:07:06,017
If you're planning to use only
your pinky in this showdown,

106
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:07,977
then I've got a couple of rules of my own.

107
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:10,437
You can take your rules
and shove them, fool!

108
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:12,814
Rules are wasted on a pup kid like you!

109
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:16,550
Ah!

110
00:07:16,633 --> 00:07:17,640
You damn bastard!

111
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:19,040
How dare you!

112
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:21,837
Well, you did say that
rules are wasted on me.

113
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:25,197
You also said something about bringing
me down with your pinky finger.

114
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:28,460
So what's the wannabe
rocker Otoishi gonna do now?

115
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:30,240
I'll kill you!

116
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,694
You already said that!

117
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:34,035
Don't you have any new material, fool?

118
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:38,080
The pain in my finger is unbearable!

119
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:40,540
I have to redirect it onto something!

120
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:45,940
This gnawing rage, I
have defense to someone!

121
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:12,770
Awesome!

122
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:23,160
First I'll kill you, then the old gas bag!

123
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:25,860
After that, your precious mommies!

124
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:30,600
That was pure ecstasy.

125
00:08:30,900 --> 00:08:32,280
My heart is free again.

126
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:36,522
There's no greater euphoria than
letting your blistering rage fly.

127
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:39,140
Let's test that theory, Otoishi!

128
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:44,580
What the hell?

129
00:08:44,900 --> 00:08:45,757
How'd he...

130
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:50,420
I know Stans can move at incredible
speeds, but this is different.

131
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:53,545
It's like he found a way
to teleport behind me.

132
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:55,837
No, Josuke, that's not what happened.

133
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:58,273
I was able to see everything back there.

134
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:00,457
Otoishi didn't take a single step.

135
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,658
You're the one who changed position.

136
00:09:02,780 --> 00:09:04,920
Something moved you. Say what?

137
00:09:05,340 --> 00:09:09,037
Chili peppers suddenly appeared and
flipped shining diamond around 180 degrees.

138
00:09:09,120 --> 00:09:10,885
without you even realizing it.

139
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:14,140
Just look, you're facing the ocean.

140
00:09:14,940 --> 00:09:16,280
Chili Pepper did that?

141
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:18,960
Where is he now, Koichi?

142
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:21,200
I don't see that sparky bastard.

143
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:22,897
He's hiding underground.

144
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:25,509
He's using the storm
drains to come and go.

145
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:29,337
He popped halfway out of the
drain to turn you around.

146
00:09:29,420 --> 00:09:32,337
There must be underground electrical
lines running all over the place.

147
00:09:32,420 --> 00:09:36,817
A little soul searching always gives
me the boost I need to bring the pain.

148
00:09:36,900 --> 00:09:38,429
Behind you, on your right.

149
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:45,980
He's right behind you!

150
00:09:54,740 --> 00:09:57,497
He bolts back into the electrical
wires at the last second,

151
00:09:57,580 --> 00:09:59,797
and his speed makes him hard to pin down.

152
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:01,697
Jotaro's the only one
who can keep up with him.

153
00:10:01,780 --> 00:10:02,857
What are we gonna do?

154
00:10:02,940 --> 00:10:04,057
Here in the harbor,

155
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:07,677
you don't have the luxury of digging
up asphalt and severing all the wires.

156
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:09,720
Josuke Higashkata. However,

157
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:13,297
the bigger the opening you make
in the ground with shiny diamonds,

158
00:10:13,380 --> 00:10:15,537
the easier it is to surface from below?

159
00:10:15,620 --> 00:10:17,117
and knock your lights out!

160
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:18,612
Josuke is on your right!

161
00:10:19,060 --> 00:10:19,980
No, in front!

162
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:21,430
Behind you!

163
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:22,830
No, ladies!

164
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:28,697
This is like a game of
whack-a-mole on steroids!

165
00:10:28,780 --> 00:10:32,427
I can't follow his movements at
all when he's going that fast!

166
00:10:34,660 --> 00:10:35,917
What's the matter, Josuke?

167
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,020
Can't keep your eye on the birdie!

168
00:10:40,580 --> 00:10:41,410
Josuke, no!

169
00:10:41,780 --> 00:10:43,140
Well, look at that.

170
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:44,555
Two minutes to spare.

171
00:10:44,700 --> 00:10:47,288
That gives me plenty
of time to finish this.

172
00:10:50,180 --> 00:10:54,237
Hey, Koichi, keep track of Chili
Pepper's location and call it out to me.

173
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:57,880
At this range, he's moving too
fast for my eyes to follow.

174
00:10:58,080 --> 00:11:00,337
But if you can't follow
him, how am I supposed to?

175
00:11:00,420 --> 00:11:02,397
As soon as I find him, he disappears.

176
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:04,656
Then you have to look harder, Koichi.

177
00:11:04,820 --> 00:11:08,879
We're about to win this and by now
you should know what I'm thinking.

178
00:11:09,620 --> 00:11:10,460
I should?

179
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:17,315
That muck on the ground, the
asphalt's turned into tar.

180
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:21,515
And the drains are covered
in all the oil from the tar.

181
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:22,840
I get it now.

182
00:11:23,060 --> 00:11:27,537
When Josuke struck the ground, he reduced
the asphalt to its most basic ingredients.

183
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:28,580
Which means...

184
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:32,413
Behind you on the left!

185
00:11:35,260 --> 00:11:37,140
Oh, yeah!

186
00:11:37,380 --> 00:11:38,556
Right in the kisser!

187
00:11:39,580 --> 00:11:40,698
Well, that's great.

188
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:42,901
Our strategy worked like a charm.

189
00:11:43,660 --> 00:11:47,836
Guess I'm the superstar now, because
I'm gonna rock this loser's world.

190
00:11:57,360 --> 00:11:58,190
Huh?

191
00:11:58,300 --> 00:11:59,280
It's the boat!

192
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:01,800
He's dead ahead, Jotaro! See?

193
00:12:02,020 --> 00:12:02,850
We're almost there!

194
00:12:02,933 --> 00:12:04,449
Don't drop your cards yet.

195
00:12:05,400 --> 00:12:06,230
Whoa!

196
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:08,576
What the hell's happening over there?

197
00:12:08,840 --> 00:12:10,280
Josuke! Koichi!

198
00:12:13,020 --> 00:12:14,079
What's that light?

199
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:17,180
I underestimated you, Josuke Higashikata.

200
00:12:17,460 --> 00:12:21,377
I was too focused on my presentation and
should have just gone in for the kill.

201
00:12:21,460 --> 00:12:23,048
But I've learned my lesson.

202
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:25,000
The juvenile me is no more.

203
00:12:25,220 --> 00:12:27,280
I'm reborn as a killing machine!

204
00:12:28,160 --> 00:12:30,400
And for my first act of anarchy,

205
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:33,557
I'll focus all of Morio's
electricity into Jelly Pepper.

206
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:34,993
This is my last resort.

207
00:12:35,260 --> 00:12:39,137
Using this technique means temporarily
knocking out power all over town,

208
00:12:39,220 --> 00:12:42,060
which I'm forced to draw
on for my lifeblood.

209
00:12:42,680 --> 00:12:44,580
But none of that matters now.

210
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:46,897
After I've done away with you cretins,

211
00:12:46,980 --> 00:12:49,197
I'll bolt over to the RC plane's battery,

212
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:52,221
then I'll fly over to
Joseph and slide his throat!

213
00:12:53,620 --> 00:12:54,450
What the?

214
00:12:54,533 --> 00:12:55,720
I can't see a thing!

215
00:12:58,420 --> 00:12:59,250
Bastards!

216
00:13:11,940 --> 00:13:13,760
I don't believe it!

217
00:13:14,040 --> 00:13:16,158
Chili Pepper got the best of Josuke!

218
00:13:20,760 --> 00:13:21,590
Josuke!

219
00:13:24,980 --> 00:13:26,457
Is it sinking in yet?

220
00:13:26,540 --> 00:13:30,000
This entire town's electrical
power is at my disposal.

221
00:13:30,900 --> 00:13:32,917
And to really drive the point home?

222
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,757
I'll be sure to charge my electric bill.

223
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:36,605
for the month to your address.

224
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:41,020
It slides out, Josuke!

225
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:46,280
Is that a tire?

226
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:51,000
Just as I expected.

227
00:13:51,320 --> 00:13:53,438
You were too dense to figure it out.

228
00:13:54,940 --> 00:13:55,770
Huh?

229
00:13:56,540 --> 00:13:57,540
Now I understand!

230
00:13:57,680 --> 00:13:59,337
You blew up that tire on purpose!

231
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:02,157
It was all part of your plan
to entomb my stand in rubber!

232
00:14:02,240 --> 00:14:03,070
Of course!

233
00:14:03,180 --> 00:14:06,417
Rubber is an insulator, so it
doesn't conduct electricity!

234
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:08,557
Chili Pepper is powerless in there!

235
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:09,640
Damn it all!

236
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:11,310
Alright!

237
00:14:11,393 --> 00:14:12,997
We just have to wait for Jojaro now!

238
00:14:13,080 --> 00:14:13,910
Just kidding!

239
00:14:15,040 --> 00:14:18,540
A good idea, but that's
not gonna work on me! Ha!

240
00:14:18,780 --> 00:14:21,857
Your plan might have succeeded
had the rubber been a meter thick!

241
00:14:21,940 --> 00:14:25,057
But this flimsy excuse for a trap
doesn't even register as a threat!

242
00:14:25,140 --> 00:14:28,320
So let me show you some
real power, dumbass!

243
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:34,280
You've lost this battle, Josuke!

244
00:14:36,640 --> 00:14:37,660
Just great.

245
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,057
You really are as stupid as you look.

246
00:14:40,140 --> 00:14:44,177
Having your stand break through the tire
was the dumbest thing you could have done.

247
00:14:44,260 --> 00:14:45,090
Huh?

248
00:14:46,520 --> 00:14:47,350
Huh?

249
00:14:47,440 --> 00:14:49,680
I forgot about the air in the tire!

250
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:52,684
The pressure release
launched him like a rocket!

251
00:14:56,700 --> 00:14:57,530
No!

252
00:14:57,613 --> 00:14:58,443
Not the ocean!

253
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:00,300
Anything but the ocean!

254
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:02,320
Oh, yeah, that's right.

255
00:15:02,880 --> 00:15:04,762
Salt water conducts electricity.

256
00:15:04,900 --> 00:15:08,977
And in the ocean, the electricity that
powers him will scatter in every direction.

257
00:15:09,060 --> 00:15:10,884
I'm sorry, I tried to kill you!

258
00:15:11,060 --> 00:15:12,797
Please, just get me outta here!

259
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:16,877
Didn't you say something about getting
rid of your juvenile self a while back?

260
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:20,000
Sorry, that's impossible
for a lowlife like you.

261
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:27,390
I'm...

262
00:15:27,473 --> 00:15:28,303
dissolving it!

263
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:33,524
His stance been completely diffused,
which means that Akira is...

264
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:40,870
Is...

265
00:15:40,953 --> 00:15:41,783
is he dead?

266
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:48,610
Jotaro!

267
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:51,000
I have some great news!

268
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:54,117
It wasn't easy, but we managed
to defeat Chili Pepper's user!

269
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,260
Nice job.

270
00:15:55,620 --> 00:15:57,149
We can breathe easier now.

271
00:15:58,340 --> 00:16:01,460
So, this old geezer is Josuke's dad, huh?

272
00:16:02,020 --> 00:16:04,297
He's kind of buff, but at the same time,

273
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:07,027
it looks like he's got
one foot in the grave.

274
00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:09,010
You.

275
00:16:09,093 --> 00:16:10,800
I don't believe we've met.

276
00:16:11,420 --> 00:16:12,773
Don't just stand there.

277
00:16:12,860 --> 00:16:13,978
Introduce yourself.

278
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:16,520
I'm Okuyasu, sir. Okuyasu?

279
00:16:16,760 --> 00:16:20,177
I live in Josuke's neighborhood,
and I'm also a stand user.

280
00:16:20,260 --> 00:16:21,090
Hmm?

281
00:16:21,173 --> 00:16:23,220
I'm a stand user! Huh? Huh?

282
00:16:23,740 --> 00:16:25,700
I said I'm a stand user!

283
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:29,057
Yeah, you're a second-hand computer?

284
00:16:29,140 --> 00:16:30,360
I'm a stand user!

285
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:32,460
Oh, a stand user.

286
00:16:32,780 --> 00:16:36,017
You young folks should really learn
to speak up and quit mumbling.

287
00:16:36,100 --> 00:16:39,660
By the way, Osumatsu, I
can't seem to find my cane.

288
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:43,035
You wouldn't happen to know
where I left it, would you?

289
00:16:43,220 --> 00:16:44,480
Oops, silly me.

290
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:47,980
I'm holding the damn thing
right here in my hand.

291
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:49,700
Has he lost his marbles?

292
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:53,030
Mr.

293
00:16:53,113 --> 00:16:55,704
Joestar, I've come to
pick up your luggage, sir.

294
00:16:56,120 --> 00:16:56,950
Huh?

295
00:16:57,033 --> 00:17:01,255
If it wouldn't be too much trouble,
would you mind answering a question?

296
00:17:02,080 --> 00:17:04,400
Has Josuke ever mentioned me to you?

297
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:09,386
The man who went 16 years without knowing
he had a son out there who needed him?

298
00:17:09,740 --> 00:17:12,180
Has he said anything about me at all?

299
00:17:13,260 --> 00:17:16,880
I hate to say it, but no, he
hasn't said much about you.

300
00:17:17,720 --> 00:17:18,940
Is that so?

301
00:17:19,220 --> 00:17:21,660
I guess it's to be expected, huh?

302
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:24,340
All right!

303
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:25,920
They're finally here!

304
00:17:26,260 --> 00:17:27,917
Look, Josuke, do you see them?

305
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,160
Yeah, cool, I guess.

306
00:17:31,100 --> 00:17:31,930
Huh?

307
00:17:32,013 --> 00:17:37,160
If I'm being honest, I kind of wish
he'd just go home and leave us in peace.

308
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:38,550
Josuke?

309
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:39,740
It's the truth.

310
00:17:39,840 --> 00:17:43,193
But don't get me wrong, I'm
glad Otoishi didn't kill him.

311
00:17:43,280 --> 00:17:45,162
Now we can go back to our lives.

312
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:46,560
Well, some of us.

313
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:49,954
I've never laid eyes on the guy before.

314
00:17:50,140 --> 00:17:52,728
How am I supposed to
think of him as my dad?

315
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:54,340
He's barely a stranger.

316
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:56,200
Just watch.

317
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:58,440
It's gonna be awkward for us both.

318
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:02,656
It's not like I hate him or anything.

319
00:18:03,100 --> 00:18:06,100
But I have to think about
my mom's well-being, too.

320
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:08,476
You get where I'm coming from, right?

321
00:18:08,900 --> 00:18:09,730
Koichi?

322
00:18:10,420 --> 00:18:11,250
No!

323
00:18:11,500 --> 00:18:12,600
It can't be!

324
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:14,190
Josuke!

325
00:18:14,273 --> 00:18:15,160
Look over there!

326
00:18:15,920 --> 00:18:17,340
His body's gone!

327
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:21,300
Jotaro, we've got trouble!

328
00:18:21,660 --> 00:18:23,780
Akira Otoishi's body disappeared!

329
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:26,080
He's still alive!

330
00:18:26,280 --> 00:18:27,515
What are we gonna do?

331
00:18:28,180 --> 00:18:29,060
Red alert!

332
00:18:29,320 --> 00:18:31,177
We've been boarded by the enemy!

333
00:18:31,260 --> 00:18:33,257
Akira Otoishi is somehow still alive!

334
00:18:33,340 --> 00:18:34,458
Are you kidding me?

335
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:36,000
Take Mr. Jot...

336
00:18:38,300 --> 00:18:39,520
Who are you?

337
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:42,488
Hey, did you say something?

338
00:18:42,700 --> 00:18:43,997
No, he...

339
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:45,600
I'm the one who said it!

340
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:49,017
I was trying to tell you that he's
not from the Speedwagon Foundation!

341
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:50,977
What the hell are you talking about?

342
00:18:51,060 --> 00:18:51,942
He's the enemy!

343
00:18:52,120 --> 00:18:53,817
So you're the guy I have to kill?

344
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:55,337
Wait, I'm on your side here!

345
00:18:55,420 --> 00:18:58,337
I'm the one who told you about the
enemy in the first place, remember?

346
00:18:58,420 --> 00:19:01,008
Would the real enemy
do something like that?

347
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:02,797
He's the one you want to beat up!

348
00:19:02,880 --> 00:19:03,777
Yeah, that makes sense!

349
00:19:03,860 --> 00:19:06,637
Surely you haven't forgotten I'm
the one who pointed out the enemy!

350
00:19:06,720 --> 00:19:08,897
This poser came here to
throw you off your guard!

351
00:19:08,980 --> 00:19:09,817
Don't fall for it!

352
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:11,417
Wait, you're making sense too!

353
00:19:11,500 --> 00:19:14,620
Then the question is, who's the user?

354
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:16,580
He's the user! Damn it!

355
00:19:16,760 --> 00:19:19,297
Why do I have to make
another important decision?

356
00:19:19,380 --> 00:19:23,417
This is what I get for relying on my
thrill for everything all these years!

357
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:25,900
Bumping off Okuyasu will be easy enough,

358
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:28,846
and thankfully Jotaro
hasn't seen my face yet.

359
00:19:29,060 --> 00:19:31,977
I just have to kill Joseph
and get the hell out of Dodge!

360
00:19:32,060 --> 00:19:32,980
It'll be easy!

361
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:35,436
These half-woods will never catch me!

362
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:36,800
It's chili pepper!

363
00:19:36,980 --> 00:19:38,440
That's not good! Huh?

364
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:40,697
You said you got me a smelly sweater!

365
00:19:40,780 --> 00:19:41,820
No thanks!

366
00:19:42,580 --> 00:19:44,100
Time to die!

367
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:56,200
I figured it out!

368
00:19:56,520 --> 00:19:57,900
The stand user

369
00:19:58,780 --> 00:20:00,497
HAS TO BE YOU!

370
00:20:00,580 --> 00:20:02,980
AHHHHH! AHHHHH!

371
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:04,510
AHHHHH!

372
00:20:05,240 --> 00:20:06,070
AHHHHH!

373
00:20:08,580 --> 00:20:10,160
Nobody fools me twice!

374
00:20:11,180 --> 00:20:13,520
Don't ever forget that you dumbass!

375
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:19,060
You figured out as a user how it was easy.

376
00:20:19,620 --> 00:20:20,920
TELL ME ALREADY!

377
00:20:21,260 --> 00:20:24,857
I was gonna beat the shit out of
both of you and sort it out later.

378
00:20:24,940 --> 00:20:27,700
That deduction stuff
is for the birds! Yeah.

379
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:03,194
You should be careful.

380
00:21:04,140 --> 00:21:07,137
One misstep and you'll be
going for an unwanted swim!

381
00:21:07,220 --> 00:21:08,057
Right?

382
00:21:08,140 --> 00:21:12,800
Sorry if I had my cane,
I could manage by myself.

383
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:15,377
But it broke a few moments ago.

384
00:21:15,460 --> 00:21:16,897
It was the strangest thing.

385
00:21:16,980 --> 00:21:20,240
Then I don't have much of a choice.

386
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:24,120
Here you can hold on to me.

387
00:21:42,260 --> 00:21:44,240
Hey, I just had a great idea!

388
00:21:44,900 --> 00:21:47,097
Josuke should have his
shining diamond fix the cane!

389
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:49,340
Do you even hear yourself, Okuyasu?

390
00:21:49,740 --> 00:21:51,777
Sometimes it's like
you don't have a brain!

391
00:21:51,860 --> 00:21:53,300
It is, but why?

392
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:55,649
Come on, isn't it obvious?

393
00:21:56,380 --> 00:21:59,500
Just this once, it's
better to leave it broken.

394
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:03,680
But why? Seriously?

395
00:22:05,840 --> 00:22:09,460
Now, if we can retrieve the bow
and arrow, it'll all be over.

396
00:22:10,040 --> 00:22:12,440
And this town will be safe again.

397
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:55,857
Don't mind a magenta feeling.

398
00:22:55,940 --> 00:22:57,457
Take a shelter in the face of my spine.

399
00:22:57,540 --> 00:22:58,857
Straight like a Chaka cherry cola.

400
00:22:58,940 --> 00:23:00,297
I don't need to try to explain.

401
00:23:00,380 --> 00:23:01,497
How to hold on tight.

402
00:23:01,580 --> 00:23:02,537
And if it happens again.

403
00:23:02,620 --> 00:23:03,797
I'ma move so slightly.

404
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:05,417
To the arms and the lips and the face.

405
00:23:05,500 --> 00:23:06,697
To the humic and the ball.

406
00:23:06,780 --> 00:23:08,017
That I need to, I want to.

407
00:23:08,100 --> 00:23:10,197
Come and stand a little bit closer.

408
00:23:10,280 --> 00:23:12,477
Breathe in and get a bit higher.

409
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:14,597
You'll never know what hit you.

410
00:23:14,680 --> 00:23:16,957
When I get to you.

411
00:23:17,040 --> 00:23:18,797
Ooh, I want you.

412
00:23:18,880 --> 00:23:21,217
I don't know if I need you.

413
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:24,400
But ooh, I've got to find you.

414
00:23:25,960 --> 00:23:27,960
Ooh, I want you.

415
00:23:28,300 --> 00:23:30,280
I don't know if I need you.

416
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:33,440
But ooh, I've got to find you.
